WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:11.090
"A talking cat!" Carabas said.

2
00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:13.652
"That's amazing!"

3
00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:18.662
Puss waved a paw. "Talking is easy."

4
00:00:18.663 --> 00:00:22.865
"But how can you talk?" Carabas asked.

5
00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:26.283
"It doesn't matter," Puss said.

6
00:00:26.284 --> 00:00:29.511
"I have a plan to help you."

7
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:33.081
Carabas stared at the cat.

8
00:00:33.082 --> 00:00:37.731
"Puss is a very unusual cat," he thought.

9
00:00:37.732 --> 00:00:42.479
"Perhaps he really can help me."

10
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.977
"First I need a bag and some boots," Puss said.

11
00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:50.028
"But plain boots are no good.

12
00:00:50.029 --> 00:00:53.210
My boots must be fancy."

13
00:00:53.211 --> 00:01:00.575
Carabas looked at the coins on the table.

14
00:01:00.576 --> 00:01:04.679
"I don't have much money," Carabas said.

15
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.538
"I can't buy nice boots."

16
00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:11.459
Puss smiled. "My feet are small.

17
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.329
The boots won't cost much."

18
00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:23.212
The next day they went to the shoemaker.

19
00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:29.259
"I need a pair of boots," Carabas said.

20
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:33.154
The shoemaker looked at Carabas' feet.

21
00:01:33.155 --> 00:01:36.759
Then he told Carabas the price.

22
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.663
Carabas gulped.

23
00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:42.024
Puss stepped forward.

24
00:01:42.025 --> 00:01:53.171
"Sir, the boots are for me," he said.

25
00:01:53.172 --> 00:01:55.550
The shoemaker was shocked.

26
00:01:55.551 --> 00:01:59.422
"A talking cat! Amazing!"

27
00:01:59.423 --> 00:02:03.655
Puss shrugged. "It's not a big deal."

28
00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.661
Puss held up a foot.

29
00:02:05.662 --> 00:02:09.154
"Look. My feet are quite small."

30
00:02:09.155 --> 00:02:14.244
The shoemaker rubbed his chin.

31
00:02:14.245 --> 00:02:18.929
"I can make you a pair for a few coins."

32
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.407
"Excellent," Puss said.

33
00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:24.728
"But the boots must be fancy."

34
00:02:24.729 --> 00:02:27.897
The shoemaker smiled proudly.

35
00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:34.563
"They'll be the fanciest boots in the kingdom!"

